    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0289/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_albedo_assuming_deep_snow'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Albedo is the ratio of outgoing to incoming shortwave irradiance, where \'shortwave irradiance\' means that both the incoming and outgoing radiation are integrated across the solar spectrum. A phrase assuming_condition indicates that the named quantity is the value which would obtain if all aspects of the system were unaltered except for the assumption of the circumstances specified by the condition.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0289'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0290/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0290/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0290/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_albedo_assuming_no_snow'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Albedo is the ratio of outgoing to incoming shortwave irradiance, where \'shortwave irradiance\' means that both the incoming and outgoing radiation are integrated across the solar spectrum. A phrase assuming_condition indicates that the named quantity is the value which would obtain if all aspects of the system were unaltered except for the assumption of the circumstances specified by the condition.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0290'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0295/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0295/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0295/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_diffuse_downwelling_photosynthetic_radiative_flux_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. "Photosynthetic" radiation is the part of the spectrum which is used in photosynthesis e.g. 400-700 nm. "Diffuse" radiation is radiation that has been scattered by gas molecules in the atmosphere and by particles such as cloud droplets and aerosols. The range of wavelengths could be specified precisely by the bounds of a coordinate of radiation_wavelength. When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called "irradiance". In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called "vector irradiance". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0295'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0328/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0328/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0328/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_albedo'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called "surface" means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. Albedo is the ratio of outgoing to incoming shortwave irradiance, where \'shortwave irradiance\' means that both the incoming and outgoing radiation are integrated across the solar spectrum. To specify the nature of the surface a cell_methods attribute should be supplied as described in Chapter 7.3.3 of the CF Conventions.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0328'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0345/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0345/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0345/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'soil_albedo'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Soil albedo is the albedo of the soil surface assuming no snow. Albedo is the ratio of outgoing to incoming shortwave irradiance, where \'shortwave irradiance\' means that both the incoming and outgoing radiation are integrated across the solar spectrum.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0345'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0364/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0364/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0364/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_extent'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The term sea_ice_extent means the total area of all grid cells in which the sea ice area fraction equals or exceeds a threshold, often chosen to be 15 per cent. The threshold must be specified by supplying a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of sea_ice_area_fraction. The horizontal domain over which sea ice extent is calculated is described by the associated coordinate variables and coordinate bounds or by a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of "region" supplied according to section 6.1.1 of the CF conventions. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0364'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0365/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0365/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0365/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_freeboard'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sea ice freeboard is the height of the sea-ice upper surface above the water surface. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0365'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0366/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0366/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0366/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_mass'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The horizontal domain over which sea ice mass is calculated is described by the associated coordinate variables and coordinate bounds or by a coordinate variable or scalar coordinate variable with the standard name of "region" supplied according to section 6.1.1 of the CF conventions."Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0366'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0367/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0367/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0367/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_speed'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Speed is the magnitude of velocity. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0367'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0369/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0369/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0369/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_thickness'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Thickness" means the vertical extent of a layer. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0369'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0371/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0371/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0371/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_volume'@en ;
    skos:definition '"X_volume" means the volume occupied by X within the grid cell. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0371'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0372/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0372/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0372/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_x_velocity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A velocity is a vector quantity. "x" indicates a vector component along the grid x-axis, positive with increasing x. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0372'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0373/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0373/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0373/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_y_velocity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A velocity is a vector quantity. "y" indicates a vector component along the grid y-axis, positive with increasing y. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0373'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0422/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0422/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0422/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '"Amount" means mass per unit area. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0422'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0423/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0423/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0423/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_area'@en ;
    skos:definition '"X_area" means the horizontal area occupied by X within the grid cell. The extent of an individual grid cell is defined by the horizontal coordinates and any associated coordinate bounds or by a string valued auxiliary coordinate variable with a standard name of "region". "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0423'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0425/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0425/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0425/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_ice_draft'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sea ice draft is the depth of the sea-ice lower surface below the water surface. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0425'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0479/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0479/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0479/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'planetary_albedo'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Albedo is the ratio of outgoing to incoming shortwave irradiance, where \'shortwave irradiance\' means that both the incoming and outgoing radiation are integrated across the solar spectrum.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0479'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0493/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0493/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0493/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'northward_sea_ice_velocity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A velocity is a vector quantity. "Northward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). Sea ice velocity is defined as a two-dimensional vector, with no vertical component. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0493'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0649/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0649/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0649/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_sea_ice_velocity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A velocity is a vector quantity. "Eastward" indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Sea ice velocity is defined as a two-dimensional vector, with no vertical component. "Sea ice" means all ice floating in the sea which has formed from freezing sea water, rather than by other processes such as calving of land ice to form icebergs.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0649'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0660/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0660/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0660/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_shortwave_flux_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. The term "shortwave" means shortwave radiation. When thought of as being incident on a surface, a radiative flux is sometimes called "irradiance". In addition, it is identical with the quantity measured by a cosine-collector light-meter and sometimes called "vector irradiance". In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0660'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0661/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0661/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0661/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_shortwave_radiance_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. The term "shortwave" means shortwave radiation. Radiance is the radiative flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. The direction from which it is coming must be specified, for instance with a coordinate of zenith_angle. If the radiation does not depend on direction, a standard name of isotropic radiance should be chosen instead.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0661'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0670/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0670/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0670/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_spherical_irradiance_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. Spherical irradiance is the radiation incident on unit area of a hemispherical (or "2-pi") collector. It is sometimes called "scalar irradiance". The direction (up/downwelling) is specified. Radiation incident on a 4-pi collector has standard names of "omnidirectional spherical irradiance".'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0670'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0672/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0672/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0672/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_longwave_radiance_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. The term "longwave" means longwave radiation. Radiance is the radiative flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. The direction from which it is coming must be specified, for instance with a coordinate of zenith_angle. If the radiation does not depend on direction, a standard name of isotropic radiance should be chosen instead.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0672'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0673/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0673/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0673/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_photon_flux_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. A photon flux is specified in terms of numbers of photons expressed in moles. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0673'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0674/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0674/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0674/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_photon_radiance_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. Photon radiance is the photon flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. The direction from which it is coming must be specified, for instance with a coordinate of zenith_angle. If the radiation does not depend on direction, a standard name of isotropic radiance should be chosen instead. A photon flux is specified in terms of numbers of photons expressed in moles.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0674'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0675/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0675/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0675/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_photon_spherical_irradiance_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. Photon spherical irradiance is the photon flux incident on unit area of a hemispherical (or "2-pi") collector. Radiation incident on a 4-pi collector has a standard name referring to "omnidirectional spherical irradiance". A photon flux is specified in terms of numbers of photons expressed in moles.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0675'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0676/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0676/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0676/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_photosynthetic_photon_flux_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. "Photosynthetic" radiation is the part of the spectrum which is used in photosynthesis e.g. 400-700 nm. The range of wavelengths could be specified precisely by the bounds of a coordinate of radiation_wavelength. A photon flux is specified in terms of numbers of photons expressed in moles. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, "flux" implies per unit area, called "flux density" in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0676'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0677/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0677/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0677/>;
    dc:modified '2018-07-03T16:09:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downwelling_photosynthetic_photon_radiance_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Downwelling radiation is radiation from above. It does not mean "net downward". The sign convention is that "upwelling" is positive upwards and "downwelling" is positive downwards. Photon radiance is the photon flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. The direction from which it is coming must be specified, for instance with a coordinate of zenith_angle. If the radiation does not depend on direction, a standard name of isotropic radiance should be chosen instead. "Photosynthetic" radiation is the part of the spectrum which is used in photosynthesis e.g. 400-700 nm. The range of wavelengths could be specified precisely by the bounds of a coordinate of radiation_wavelength. A photon flux is specified in terms of numbers of photons expressed in moles.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0677'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0678/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0678/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
